<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila firm plans to buy U.S. wheat, soybeans.</title>
<headline>Manila firm plans to buy U.S. wheat, soybeans.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Philippine firm sought tenders on Friday for the supply of 23,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat and 15,000 tonnes of soybeans for April and May shipments, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The company said it plans to open the bids later today,&quot; a trader who was invited in the bidding told Reuters.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, the unidentified firm rejected bids for the supply of the soybeans due to high prices, traders said.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (632) 841-89-36, fax 817-62-67</p>
